import equational_theories.Definability.ExactPrune

/-!
# A searched exact-automorphism class on `Fin 9`: data

The group is `48` permutations of `Fin 9`, the excess permutations that pin it from above are `2`,
and the invariant family it acts on has `2,025` members. How many of those have this group as their
automorphism group *exactly* is not computed and does not need to be: the family is indexed by the
subtype `Magma.tup9R410` of transport tuples passing `Magma.tupOK`, and both sides of the rectangle
are decided by search rather than by enumeration. See `Definability/ExactPrune.lean` for the device
and `Definability/Srch_S9R410.lean` for the data lemmas.

This file is generated by `genrect.py`; it holds only tables, so that `native_decide` -- which
recompiles its whole enclosing module on each invocation -- never has to compile them twice.
-/

-- an array literal elaborates one recursive step per entry, and the group is one of the arrays, so
-- the depth has to grow with it: `10000` was fine up to a few hundred permutations and is not fine
-- at `1152`.  The heartbeat bump is for `tupOK` on the source exhibits below, which the kernel
-- checks: it is `|H|` endomorphism tests of `n^2` cells each.
set_option maxRecDepth 10000
set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000

namespace S9R410

